var tipuesearch = {"pages":[{"title":" daqp-fortran ","text":"daqp-fortran daqp-fortran A modern Fortran port of DAQP , the dual active-set\nsolver for dense convex quadratic programs by Daniel Arnström, with an object-oriented\ninterface. It is built with fpm and needs no C compiler. It solves min 0.5 x 'Hx + f' x s . t . blower ( 1 : ms ) <= x ( 1 : ms ) <= bupper ( 1 : ms ) ( simple bounds ) blower ( ms + 1 :) <= A x <= bupper ( ms + 1 :) ( general constraints ) with every row two-sided ( daqp_inf for no bound), and optional per-row flags for\nequality, immutable, soft, and binary constraints. All of DAQP's solvers are ported: the dual active-set method for strictly convex QPs, with warm and hot starts; a proximal-point outer loop for semidefinite QPs and LPs; branch and bound for binary constraints (mixed-integer QPs); hierarchical (lexicographic) QPs: levels of constraints, each softened and then\n  fixed at its best slack; affine variational inequalities (a nonsymmetric H ); the elimination of equality constraints (a null-space reduction, when there are\n  many equalities); soft constraints with uniform or individual weights , a prefactorized Hessian,\n  primal and dual starts, a time limit, and the removal of redundant constraints\n  ( daqp_minrep ). When to use it Small and medium dense QPs (up to a few hundred variables): the Hessian is factored\n  once per QP, and the working set's factorization is updated, not recomputed, at each\n  iteration. Sequences of similar QPs (model predictive control, SQP): new data can be given\n  without refactoring, and each solve starts from the previous working set. Convex problems only. H must be symmetric positive definite. A positive\n  semidefinite H (including H = 0 , or no H : an LP) is handled by a proximal-point\n  outer loop. An indefinite H is reported as daqp_nonconvex . Large sparse problems\n  are better served by a sparse solver. Usage use daqp_module type ( daqp_type ) :: qp real ( daqp_wp ) :: x ( n ), lam ( m ) integer :: istat call qp % setup ( H , f , A , bupper , blower , istat ) ! factor H, form the problem call qp % solve ( x , lam , istat ) ! istat > 0: solved call qp % update ( istat , f = f2 , bupper = bu2 ) ! new data, same sizes call qp % solve ( x , lam , istat ) ! hot start from the previous working set H(n,n) , f(n) , A(m-ms,n) in the usual Fortran (column-major) layout, and bounds bupper(m) , blower(m) . The number of simple bounds is ms = m - size(A,1) : the first ms entries of the bounds apply to x(1:ms) . H , f , and A are optional (use\n  keyword arguments after an omitted one): no H is an LP, no A means only simple bounds. Options are components of daqp_type (upstream's settings, with its defaults): primal_tol , dual_tol , zero_tol , pivot_tol , progress_tol , cycle_tol , iter_limit , fval_bound , eps_prox , eta_prox , rho_soft , w_soft , rel_subopt , abs_subopt , sing_tol , refactor_tol , time_limit , eq_reduction . set_defaults restores them. Results of the latest solve: qp%status , qp%iter , qp%fval , qp%soft_slack , qp%outer_iter (nodes of the branch and bound, or outer iterations), qp%solve_time , qp%setup_time (or qp%info(...) ). Constraint flags: sense(m) in setup , with daqp_equality (or simply equal bounds), daqp_immutable , daqp_soft , daqp_binary . Other arguments of setup : break_points (a hierarchical QP: the last constraint of\n  each level), is_avi (an AVI), R (the Cholesky factor of H , packed by rows, instead\n  of H ), primal_start , dual_start . qp%set_soft_weights(istat, rho_l, rho_u, w_l, w_u) sets individual weights of the soft\n  constraints; qp%set_primal_start(x, istat) a starting point (for binary constraints,\n  an incumbent). daqp_type is copyable (allocatable components only), and allocates nothing during solve . See example/example_simple.f90 and example/example_mpc.f90 . Multipliers lam satisfies with : lam(i) > 0 when the upper bound of row i is active, lam(i) < 0 when its lower bound\nis active, 0 when inactive. daqp_lower_positive(lam) converts to the convention at a lower bound ( ). Warm and hot starts By default, solve starts from the working set of the previous solve (a hot start );\n  after setup , from the equality constraints only. qp%get_working_set(active, at_lower) returns the working set of a solution; qp%solve(x, lam, istat, active=active, at_lower=at_lower) (or set_working_set )\n  starts from a given one (a warm start ). Rows that are linearly dependent on the others\n  are dropped. qp%solve(..., cold=.true.) starts from the empty working set. update with new f or bounds keeps the factorization of H and the working set; with\n  a new A , the problem is formed again but H is not refactored; with a new H ,\n  everything is recomputed. Soft constraints A row flagged daqp_soft may be violated: a violation s (of the normalized row) adds w_soft*s + s**2/(2*rho_soft) to the objective ( w_soft = 0 by default: a quadratic\npenalty; a large enough w_soft gives an exact penalty). Individual weights per row and\nside ( set_soft_weights ) are in the units of the problem. The exit status is then daqp_soft_optimal and qp%soft_slack is the largest violation. Binary constraints, hierarchies, AVIs A row flagged daqp_binary must be active at one of its bounds (for a binary variable,\n  bounds 0 and 1 on a simple bound). The problem is solved by branch and bound, which\n  needs a strictly convex objective; rel_subopt and abs_subopt allow a suboptimal\n  solution, and set_primal_start gives an incumbent. With break_points , the constraints form levels (the first is hard). Each next level\n  is minimized as soft constraints and then fixed at its slacks; lam returns the slacks. With is_avi = .true. , the solver finds x in the feasible set with (Hx + f)'(y - x) >= 0 for every feasible y , for a nonsymmetric H (Douglas-Rachford\n  splitting with Newton steps). daqp_avi solves one in a single call. Elimination of equalities With many equality constraints, they can be eliminated before the solve (a QR null-space\nreduction; the solution and all the multipliers are those of the original problem). eq_reduction = daqp_eq_reduction_auto (the default) does so in daqp_quadprog when it\npays off, daqp_eq_reduction_on always (also for setup + solve ), and daqp_eq_reduction_off never. Statuses status value meaning daqp_success 0 setup / update succeeded daqp_optimal 1 solved daqp_soft_optimal 2 solved, a soft constraint is violated daqp_no_freedom 3 hierarchical QP: a level failed; the solution of the levels before daqp_optimal_inexact 4 solved after persistent cycling; violates a constraint by more than primal_tol daqp_infeasible -1 infeasible daqp_cycling -2 cycling daqp_unbounded -3 unbounded (LP) daqp_iteration_limit -4 iteration limit daqp_nonconvex -5 H is not positive (semi)definite daqp_overdetermined -6 inconsistent equalities in the initial working set daqp_time_limit -7 the time limit was reached daqp_unsupported -8 unsupported combination (a hierarchy with a singular H , or a re-solve of a hierarchy without an update) daqp_invalid_input -101 invalid sizes or indices daqp_out_of_memory -102 an allocation failed (or the problem is too large) daqp_not_setup -103 setup was not called, or failed Low-level interface daqp_core holds the one-to-one port (a workspace type and plain procedures: daqp_setup , daqp_solve , daqp_update_ldp , daqp_quadprog , daqp_avi , daqp_minrep , daqp_ldp , daqp_bnb , daqp_hiqp , ...), with the same algorithm, order of operations,\nand tolerances as the C code; daqp_eq_elim the elimination of equalities, and daqp_types the types and constants. daqp_setup also accepts A in its internal layout\n( At(n,m-ms) , a row of A per column), which saves a transposed copy. Real kinds The real kind is chosen by a preprocessor flag: -DREAL32 , -DREAL64 (the default), or -DREAL128 , e.g. fpm test --flag \"-DREAL128\" . In double and quadruple precision the\ndefault tolerances and constants are upstream's; in single precision, those below a few epsilon (the tolerances, rho_soft , eps_prox , and the tolerances of the primal and\ndual starts) are raised to a multiple of epsilon . In single precision, LPs (solved by\nthe proximal-point loop) are less reliable: about 2% of random LPs end with daqp_cycling , whose rounding errors swamp the progress test of the cycle guard. Install [dependencies] daqp-fortran = { git = \"https://github.com/jacobwilliams/daqp-fortran\" } To build and test: fpm test . To build the documentation: ford ford.md . Comparison with the C code The upstream C repository is a git submodule in upstream/daqp , pinned to the release the\nport follows (v0.10.3). It is only needed for the comparison, not to use the package\n( git clone --recursive , or git submodule update --init ). tools / run_compare . sh # writes compare/RESULTS.md tools / run_compare . sh quick # a short check (CI) tools/build_upstream.sh builds the C library into build/upstream/libdaqp.a ; compare/ is a separate fpm project that solves the same problems with both (upstream's\ntest problems, random QPs of sizes 2 to 500 and condition numbers up to 1e10, degenerate,\ninfeasible, semidefinite, soft, LP, warm-start sequences, the elimination of equalities,\nbranch and bound, hierarchical QPs, AVIs, prefactorized Hessians, primal and dual starts,\nindividual soft weights, and redundant constraints: over a thousand problems) and compares\nexit flags, iteration counts, working sets, solutions, multipliers, objectives, KKT\nresiduals, and speed. With fused multiply-adds disabled in both builds, the port gives bit-for-bit the\nsame results as the C code on every problem; the optimized builds agree to round-off, and\nrun at the same speed (see compare/RESULTS.md ). Not ported Upstream's code generation ( codegen/ , which writes C source files of a workspace for\nembedded targets), and its interfaces to other languages (Julia, Python, MATLAB, C++,\nSimulink). Licence MIT (see LICENSE ). DAQP is MIT-licensed, Copyright (c) 2022 Daniel Arnström;\nthis package is a derivative work (see NOTICE ). Reference D. Arnström, A. Bemporad, D. Axehill, A dual active-set solver for embedded quadratic\nprogramming using recursive LDLᵀ updates , IEEE Transactions on Automatic Control 67(8),\n4362–4369, 2022. Developer Info Jacob Williams","tags":"home","url":"index.html"},{"title":"daqp_type – daqp-fortran ","text":"type, public :: daqp_type A DAQP solver for one problem (copyable). Inherits type~~daqp_type~~InheritsGraph type~daqp_type daqp_type type~daqp_workspace daqp_workspace type~daqp_type->type~daqp_workspace work type~daqp_avi_data daqp_avi_data type~daqp_workspace->type~daqp_avi_data avi type~daqp_bnb_data daqp_bnb_data type~daqp_workspace->type~daqp_bnb_data bnb type~daqp_eq_data daqp_eq_data type~daqp_workspace->type~daqp_eq_data eq type~daqp_problem daqp_problem type~daqp_workspace->type~daqp_problem qp type~daqp_settings daqp_settings type~daqp_workspace->type~daqp_settings settings type~daqp_node daqp_node type~daqp_bnb_data->type~daqp_node tree type~daqp_ldp_data daqp_ldp_data type~daqp_eq_data->type~daqp_ldp_data other type~daqp_vec daqp_vec type~daqp_eq_data->type~daqp_vec cols type~daqp_ldp_data->type~daqp_problem qp Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), public :: primal_tol = daqp_default_prim_tol tolerance for primal feasibility real(kind=wp), public :: dual_tol = daqp_default_dual_tol tolerance for dual feasibility real(kind=wp), public :: zero_tol = daqp_default_zero_tol values below are regarded as zero real(kind=wp), public :: pivot_tol = daqp_default_pivot_tol pivots of the LDL' below are reordered real(kind=wp), public :: progress_tol = daqp_default_prog_tol minimum objective progress (cycle guard) integer(kind=ip), public :: cycle_tol = daqp_default_cycle_tol iterations without progress before cycling is assumed integer(kind=ip), public :: iter_limit = daqp_default_iter_limit maximum number of iterations real(kind=wp), public :: fval_bound = daqp_inf the problem is regarded as infeasible if the objective exceeds this real(kind=wp), public :: eps_prox = daqp_default_eps_prox proximal regularization (negative: automatic, only if H is singular) real(kind=wp), public :: eta_prox = daqp_default_eta tolerance of the proximal loop (negative: automatic) real(kind=wp), public :: rho_soft = daqp_default_rho_soft soft constraints: the penalty is s**2/(2*rho_soft) per unit slack s (normalized) real(kind=wp), public :: w_soft = daqp_default_w_soft soft constraints: linear penalty w_soft*s (0: purely quadratic) real(kind=wp), public :: rel_subopt = 0.0_wp branch and bound: relative suboptimality tolerance real(kind=wp), public :: abs_subopt = 0.0_wp branch and bound: absolute suboptimality tolerance real(kind=wp), public :: sing_tol = daqp_default_sing_tol pivots below mark a singular working set real(kind=wp), public :: refactor_tol = daqp_default_refactor_tol pivots below trigger a refactorization at a solution real(kind=wp), public :: time_limit = 0.0_wp time limit of a solve [s] (0: none) integer(kind=ip), public :: eq_reduction = daqp_eq_reduction_auto elimination of equalities: daqp_eq_reduction_off , _auto (for a solve from scratch, if worthwhile: daqp_quadprog ), _on integer(kind=ip), public :: status = daqp_not_setup status of the latest call integer(kind=ip), public :: iter = 0 iterations integer(kind=ip), public :: outer_iter = 0 nodes (branch and bound), or outer iterations (proximal, AVI) real(kind=wp), public :: fval = 0.0_wp objective function value real(kind=wp), public :: soft_slack = 0.0_wp largest violation of a soft constraint real(kind=wp), public :: solve_time = 0.0_wp time of the latest solve [s] real(kind=wp), public :: setup_time = 0.0_wp time of the latest setup [s] type( daqp_workspace ), private :: work the solver's workspace Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: setup private  subroutine setup (me, H, f, A, bupper, blower, istat, ms, sense, break_points, is_avi, R, primal_start, dual_start) Set up the solver for a problem: factor H and form the LDP. Call once per\nproblem (or after a change of the dimensions). Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( daqp_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional, contiguous :: H (:,:) Hessian (n,n) , symmetric (absent: an LP;\nnonsymmetric with is_avi ) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional, contiguous :: f (:) linear term (n) (absent: zero) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional, contiguous :: A (:,:) general constraints (m-ms,n) (absent: only simple bounds) real(kind=wp), intent(in), contiguous :: bupper (:) upper bounds (m) ( daqp_inf for none) real(kind=wp), intent(in), contiguous :: blower (:) lower bounds (m) ( -daqp_inf for none) integer(kind=ip), intent(out) :: istat daqp_success or a negative status integer(kind=ip), intent(in), optional :: ms number of simple bounds (checked if present) integer(kind=ip), intent(in), optional, contiguous :: sense (:) constraint flags (m) ( daqp_equality , daqp_soft , daqp_binary , ...) integer(kind=ip), intent(in), optional :: break_points (:) hierarchical QP: the last constraint of each level\n(increasing, ending with m ; the first level is hard) logical, intent(in), optional :: is_avi solve the affine variational inequality defined by H and f real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional, contiguous :: R (:) instead of H : its upper Cholesky factor ( H = R'R ),\npacked by rows ( n(n+1)/2 ) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional, contiguous :: primal_start (:) a primal start (n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional, contiguous :: dual_start (:) a dual start (m) (DAQP's sign convention) procedure, public :: solve private  subroutine solve (me, x, lam, istat, active, at_lower, cold) Solve the problem. By default, the solve starts from the working set of the\nprevious solve (a hot start, which suits a sequence of similar problems),\nor from the equality constraints only, after setup . Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( daqp_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: x (:) solution (n) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: lam (:) multipliers (m) (see the module documentation for the sign) integer(kind=ip), intent(out) :: istat status (positive: solved) integer(kind=ip), intent(in), optional :: active (:) warm start: indices of the active constraints logical, intent(in), optional :: at_lower (:) warm start: whether each is at its lower bound (default: upper) logical, intent(in), optional :: cold start from the equality constraints only procedure, public :: update private  subroutine update (me, istat, H, f, A, bupper, blower, sense) Replace the data of the problem (same dimensions), and recompute only what\ndepends on it: a new H refactors; new f or bounds keep the\nfactorizations and the working set (for a hot start). A new sense replaces the constraint flags (and restarts the working set from them). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( daqp_type ), intent(inout) :: me integer(kind=ip), intent(out) :: istat daqp_success or a negative status real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: H (:,:) new Hessian (n,n) (only if one was given to setup ) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: f (:) new linear term (n) (only if one was given to setup ) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: A (:,:) new general constraints (m-ms,n) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: bupper (:) new upper bounds (m) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: blower (:) new lower bounds (m) integer(kind=ip), intent(in), optional :: sense (:) new constraint flags (m) procedure, public :: set_working_set private  subroutine set_working_set (me, active, istat, at_lower) Set the working set for the next solve (a warm start). The indices must\nbe distinct and in 1..m ; equality constraints are always active.\nConstraints that are linearly dependent on the others are dropped. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( daqp_type ), intent(inout) :: me integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: active (:) indices of the active constraints integer(kind=ip), intent(out) :: istat daqp_success or a negative status logical, intent(in), optional :: at_lower (:) whether each is at its lower bound (default: upper) procedure, public :: get_working_set private  subroutine get_working_set (me, active, at_lower) The working set at the latest solution (for a later warm start). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( daqp_type ), intent(in) :: me integer(kind=ip), intent(out), allocatable :: active (:) indices of the active constraints logical, intent(out), allocatable :: at_lower (:) whether each is at its lower bound procedure, public :: set_primal_start private  subroutine set_primal_start (me, x, istat) Set the starting primal iterate (for a problem with binary constraints, a\ncandidate solution, used as the incumbent if it is feasible). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( daqp_type ), intent(inout) :: me real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x (:) iterate (n) integer(kind=ip), intent(out) :: istat daqp_success or a negative status procedure, public :: set_soft_weights private  subroutine set_soft_weights (me, istat, rho_l, rho_u, w_l, w_u) Set individual weights of the soft constraints (one entry per constraint;\nzero selects rho_soft / w_soft ; an absent argument leaves that weight as it\nis). A violation s of the lower (upper) side of a soft constraint adds w_l*s + s**2/(2*rho_l) ( w_u*s + s**2/(2*rho_u) ) to the objective\n(in the units of the problem). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( daqp_type ), intent(inout) :: me integer(kind=ip), intent(out) :: istat daqp_success or a negative status real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: rho_l (:) reciprocal quadratic weights of the lower sides (m) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: rho_u (:) reciprocal quadratic weights of the upper sides (m) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: w_l (:) linear weights of the lower sides (m) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: w_u (:) linear weights of the upper sides (m) procedure, public :: info private  subroutine info (me, status, iter, outer_iter, fval, soft_slack, n_active, solve_time, setup_time) Information on the latest solve. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( daqp_type ), intent(in) :: me integer(kind=ip), intent(out), optional :: status status of the latest call integer(kind=ip), intent(out), optional :: iter iterations integer(kind=ip), intent(out), optional :: outer_iter nodes (branch and bound), or outer iterations real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional :: fval objective function value real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional :: soft_slack largest violation of a soft constraint integer(kind=ip), intent(out), optional :: n_active number of active constraints real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional :: solve_time time of the latest solve [s] real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional :: setup_time time of the latest setup [s] procedure, public :: set_defaults private  subroutine set_defaults (me) Restore the default options. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( daqp_type ), intent(inout) :: me procedure, public :: destroy private  subroutine destroy (me) Free the memory (the options are kept). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( daqp_type ), intent(inout) :: me procedure, public :: n_variables private pure function n_variables (me) Number of variables (0 if not set up). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( daqp_type ), intent(in) :: me Return Value integer(kind=ip) procedure, public :: n_constraints private pure function n_constraints (me) Number of constraints, including the simple bounds (0 if not set up). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( daqp_type ), intent(in) :: me Return Value integer(kind=ip) procedure, private :: copy_settings private  subroutine copy_settings (me) Copy the options into the workspace. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( daqp_type ), intent(inout) :: me Source Code type , public :: daqp_type !! A DAQP solver for one problem (copyable). ! options (upstream's settings, with its defaults) real ( wp ) :: primal_tol = daqp_default_prim_tol !! tolerance for primal feasibility real ( wp ) :: dual_tol = daqp_default_dual_tol !! tolerance for dual feasibility real ( wp ) :: zero_tol = daqp_default_zero_tol !! values below are regarded as zero real ( wp ) :: pivot_tol = daqp_default_pivot_tol !! pivots of the `LDL'` below are reordered real ( wp ) :: progress_tol = daqp_default_prog_tol !! minimum objective progress (cycle guard) integer ( ip ) :: cycle_tol = daqp_default_cycle_tol !! iterations without progress before cycling is assumed integer ( ip ) :: iter_limit = daqp_default_iter_limit !! maximum number of iterations real ( wp ) :: fval_bound = daqp_inf !! the problem is regarded as infeasible if the objective exceeds this real ( wp ) :: eps_prox = daqp_default_eps_prox !! proximal regularization (negative: automatic, only if `H` is singular) real ( wp ) :: eta_prox = daqp_default_eta !! tolerance of the proximal loop (negative: automatic) real ( wp ) :: rho_soft = daqp_default_rho_soft !! soft constraints: the penalty is `s**2/(2*rho_soft)` per unit slack `s` (normalized) real ( wp ) :: w_soft = daqp_default_w_soft !! soft constraints: linear penalty `w_soft*s` (0: purely quadratic) real ( wp ) :: rel_subopt = 0.0_wp !! branch and bound: relative suboptimality tolerance real ( wp ) :: abs_subopt = 0.0_wp !! branch and bound: absolute suboptimality tolerance real ( wp ) :: sing_tol = daqp_default_sing_tol !! pivots below mark a singular working set real ( wp ) :: refactor_tol = daqp_default_refactor_tol !!