ric interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code integer ( ip ) function update_R_qp ( work , defer_inverse ) result ( flag ) type ( daqp_workspace ), intent ( inout ) :: work !! workspace logical , intent ( in ) :: defer_inverse !! defer the inverse of the factor if ( work % qp % problem_type == daqp_problem_factored ) then flag = update_R ( work , defer_inverse , Rf = work % qp % Rf ) else if ( work % qp % has_H ) then flag = update_R ( work , defer_inverse , H = work % qp % Hc ) else flag = update_R ( work , defer_inverse ) end if end function update_R_qp","tags":"","url":"proc/update_r_qp.html"},{"title":"finish_Rinv_qp – daqp-fortran","text":"private  function finish_Rinv_qp(work) Complete the inverse of the factor of the Hessian of the problem in the workspace. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace Return Value logical Calls proc~~finish_rinv_qp~~CallsGraph proc~finish_rinv_qp finish_Rinv_qp proc~finish_rinv finish_Rinv proc~finish_rinv_qp->proc~finish_rinv proc~invert_r invert_R proc~finish_rinv->proc~invert_r proc~ridx~2 ridx proc~invert_r->proc~ridx~2 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~finish_rinv_qp~~CalledByGraph proc~finish_rinv_qp finish_Rinv_qp proc~update_ldp_core update_ldp_core proc~update_ldp_core->proc~finish_rinv_qp proc~daqp_update_ldp daqp_update_ldp proc~daqp_update_ldp->proc~update_ldp_core proc~daqp_setup daqp_setup proc~daqp_setup->proc~daqp_update_ldp proc~daqp_solve daqp_solve proc~daqp_solve->proc~daqp_update_ldp proc~update daqp_type%update proc~update->proc~daqp_update_ldp proc~daqp_quadprog daqp_quadprog proc~daqp_quadprog->proc~daqp_setup proc~daqp_quadprog->proc~daqp_solve proc~setup daqp_type%setup proc~setup->proc~daqp_setup proc~solve daqp_type%solve proc~solve->proc~daqp_solve proc~daqp_avi daqp_avi proc~daqp_avi->proc~daqp_quadprog Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code logical function finish_Rinv_qp ( work ) type ( daqp_workspace ), intent ( inout ) :: work !! workspace if ( work % qp % problem_type == daqp_problem_factored ) then finish_Rinv_qp = finish_Rinv ( work , . true .) else finish_Rinv_qp = finish_Rinv ( work , . false ., work % qp % Hc ) end if end function finish_Rinv_qp","tags":"","url":"proc/finish_rinv_qp.html"},{"title":"get_proximal_regularization – daqp-fortran","text":"private  function get_proximal_regularization(work) result(eps) The proximal regularization that the factor of H was formed with. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(in) :: work workspace Return Value real(kind=wp) Calls proc~~get_proximal_regularization~~CallsGraph proc~get_proximal_regularization get_proximal_regularization proc~has~2 has proc~get_proximal_regularization->proc~has~2 proc~hessian_scale_of hessian_scale_of proc~get_proximal_regularization->proc~hessian_scale_of proc~prox_reg_scaled prox_reg_scaled proc~get_proximal_regularization->proc~prox_reg_scaled proc~ridx~2 ridx proc~get_proximal_regularization->proc~ridx~2 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~get_proximal_regularization~~CalledByGraph proc~get_proximal_regularization get_proximal_regularization proc~daqp_prox daqp_prox proc~daqp_prox->proc~get_proximal_regularization proc~daqp_solve daqp_solve proc~daqp_solve->proc~daqp_prox proc~daqp_quadprog daqp_quadprog proc~daqp_quadprog->proc~daqp_solve proc~solve daqp_type%solve proc~solve->proc~daqp_solve proc~daqp_avi daqp_avi proc~daqp_avi->proc~daqp_quadprog Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code real ( wp ) function get_proximal_regularization ( work ) result ( eps ) type ( daqp_workspace ), intent ( in ) :: work !! workspace integer ( ip ) :: i , n real ( wp ) :: recovered , rinv eps = 0.0_wp n = work % n if ( work % n_prox == 0 . or . . not . work % has_qp ) return if (. not . work % qp % has_H ) return if ( work % rmode == rinv_diag . and . work % n_prox < n ) then i = findloc ( work % prox_mask ( 1 : n ), . true ., dim = 1 ) eps = 1.0_wp / ( work % R ( i ) * work % R ( i )) - work % qp % Hc ( i , i ) return end if if ( work % rmode == rinv_diag ) then ! diagonal regularization has no retry loop, so reproduce its ! scale-based floor directly eps = abs ( work % settings % eps_prox ) if ( work % qp % problem_type /= daqp_problem_factored ) then eps = prox_reg_scaled ( work , hessian_scale_of ( n , work % qp % Hc )) end if return end if ! semi-proximal: recover eps from a regularized row of Rinv (e_i/sqrt(eps)) if ( work % n_prox < n ) then i = findloc ( work % prox_mask ( 1 : n ), . true ., dim = 1 ) if ( i <= work % ms . and . has ( work % state , state_rinv_normalized )) then rinv = 1.0_wp / work % scaling ( i ) else rinv = work % R ( ridx ( i , i , n )) end if eps = 1.0_wp / ( rinv * rinv ) return end if ! handle the eps-shift correctly for simple bounds rinv = work % R ( 1 ) if ( work % ms > 0 ) rinv = rinv / work % scaling ( 1 ) recovered = 1.0_wp / ( rinv * rinv ) - work % qp % Hc ( 1 , 1 ) eps = prox_reg_scaled ( work , hessian_scale_of ( n , work % qp % Hc )) if ( eps <= 0.0_wp ) then eps = 0.0_wp return end if do while ( 1.5_wp * eps < recovered ) eps = eps * 2.0_wp end do end function get_proximal_regularization","tags":"","url":"proc/get_proximal_regularization.html"},{"title":"update_M – daqp-fortran","text":"private  function update_M(work) result(flag) Form M = A*Rinv (rows normalized). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace Return Value integer(kind=ip) Calls proc~~update_m~~CallsGraph proc~update_m update_M proc~daqp_reset_workspace daqp_reset_workspace proc~update_m->proc~daqp_reset_workspace proc~has~2 has proc~update_m->proc~has~2 proc~normalize_m normalize_M proc~update_m->proc~normalize_m proc~rinv_product_block rinv_product_block proc~update_m->proc~rinv_product_block proc~normalize_m->proc~has~2 proc~ridx~2 ridx proc~rinv_product_block->proc~ridx~2 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~update_m~~CalledByGraph proc~update_m update_M proc~retry_avi_with_reduced_rho retry_avi_with_reduced_rho proc~retry_avi_with_reduced_rho->proc~update_m proc~update_ldp_core update_ldp_core proc~update_ldp_core->proc~update_m proc~daqp_solve_avi daqp_solve_avi proc~daqp_solve_avi->proc~retry_avi_with_reduced_rho proc~daqp_solve_avi->proc~daqp_solve_avi proc~daqp_update_ldp daqp_update_ldp proc~daqp_update_ldp->proc~update_ldp_core proc~daqp_setup daqp_setup proc~daqp_setup->proc~daqp_update_ldp proc~daqp_solve daqp_solve proc~daqp_solve->proc~daqp_solve_avi proc~daqp_solve->proc~daqp_update_ldp proc~update daqp_type%update proc~update->proc~daqp_update_ldp proc~daqp_quadprog daqp_quadprog proc~daqp_quadprog->proc~daqp_setup proc~daqp_quadprog->proc~daqp_solve proc~setup daqp_type%setup proc~setup->proc~daqp_setup proc~solve daqp_type%solve proc~solve->proc~daqp_solve proc~daqp_avi daqp_avi proc~daqp_avi->proc~daqp_quadprog Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code integer ( ip ) function update_M ( work ) result ( flag ) type ( daqp_workspace ), intent ( inout ) :: work !! workspace integer ( ip ) :: i , j , k , n , ns , mA n = work % n mA = work % m - work % ms ! the rows of Rinv of the simple bounds are scaled if Rinv is normalized ns = 0 if ( has ( work % state , state_rinv_normalized )) ns = work % ms select case ( work % rmode ) case ( rinv_dense ) do k = 1 , mA do j = 1 , ns ! undo the scaling in Rinv work % Mr ( j , k ) = work % qp % At ( j , k ) / work % scaling ( j ) end do do j = ns + 1 , n work % Mr ( j , k ) = work % qp % At ( j , k ) end do end do ! Mr(:,k) <-- Rinv'*Mr(:,k), in place, four rows of A at a time k = 1 do while ( k + 3 <= mA ) call rinv_product_block ( work , k , 4 ) k = k + 4 end do if ( k <= mA ) call rinv_product_block ( work , k , mA - k + 1 ) case ( rinv_diag ) do k = 1 , mA do i = 1 , n work % Mr ( i , k ) = work % qp % At ( i , k ) * work % R ( i ) end do end do case default ! copy A to M do k = 1 , mA work % Mr (:, k ) = work % qp % At (:, k ) end do end select call daqp_reset_workspace ( work ) ! internal factorizations need to be redone flag = normalize_M ( work ) end function update_M","tags":"","url":"proc/update_m.html"},{"title":"check_bounds – daqp-fortran","text":"private  function check_bounds(work) result(do_activate) Check the bounds for trivial infeasibility, and detect equality constraints\n(equal bounds). Returns 1 if the working set has to be activated again,\n0, or daqp_exit_infeasible . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace Return Value integer(kind=ip) Calls proc~~check_bounds~~CallsGraph proc~check_bounds check_bounds proc~has~2 has proc~check_bounds->proc~has~2 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the fol