( has ( work % sense ( i ), daqp_immutable ) . and . . not . has ( work % sense ( i ), daqp_active )) cycle if ( i <= work % ms ) then val = work % x ( i ) else val = dot_seq ( work % n , work % qp % At (:, i - work % ms ), work % x ) end if if ( val > work % qp % bupper ( i ) + tol . or . val < work % qp % blower ( i ) - tol ) then violates_hard = . true . return end if end do end function violates_hard","tags":"","url":"proc/violates_hard.html"},{"title":"prox_is_infeasible – daqp-fortran","text":"private pure function prox_is_infeasible(work) Whether the certificate of infeasibility from daqp_ldp (the dependency lam_star of a singular working set) is valid and implies a violation above primal_tol . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(in) :: work workspace Return Value logical Calls proc~~prox_is_infeasible~~CallsGraph proc~prox_is_infeasible prox_is_infeasible proc~has~2 has proc~prox_is_infeasible->proc~has~2 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~prox_is_infeasible~~CalledByGraph proc~prox_is_infeasible prox_is_infeasible proc~daqp_prox daqp_prox proc~daqp_prox->proc~prox_is_infeasible proc~daqp_solve daqp_solve proc~daqp_solve->proc~daqp_prox proc~daqp_quadprog daqp_quadprog proc~daqp_quadprog->proc~daqp_solve proc~solve daqp_type%solve proc~solve->proc~daqp_solve proc~daqp_avi daqp_avi proc~daqp_avi->proc~daqp_quadprog Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure logical function prox_is_infeasible ( work ) type ( daqp_workspace ), intent ( in ) :: work !! workspace integer ( ip ) :: i , id logical :: lower , wrong_sign real ( wp ) :: q , gap , norm , wrong prox_is_infeasible = . false . if ( work % sing_ind == empty_ind ) return gap = 0.0_wp norm = 0.0_wp wrong = 0.0_wp do i = 1 , work % n_active id = work % WS ( i ) lower = has ( work % sense ( id ), daqp_lower ) q = work % lam_star ( i ) * work % scaling ( id ) if ( lower ) then gap = gap - q * work % qp % blower ( id ) else gap = gap - q * work % qp % bupper ( id ) end if if ( lower ) then wrong_sign = q > 0.0_wp else wrong_sign = q < 0.0_wp end if if (. not . has ( work % sense ( id ), daqp_immutable ) . and . wrong_sign ) then if ( work % qp % bupper ( id ) < daqp_inf . and . work % qp % blower ( id ) > - daqp_inf ) then gap = gap - abs ( q ) * ( work % qp % bupper ( id ) - work % qp % blower ( id )) else wrong = wrong + abs ( q ) end if end if norm = norm + abs ( q ) end do prox_is_infeasible = wrong <= 1.0e-8_wp * norm . and . gap > work % settings % primal_tol * norm end function prox_is_infeasible","tags":"","url":"proc/prox_is_infeasible.html"},{"title":"prox_project_step – daqp-fortran","text":"private  function prox_project_step(work, eps) Project the latest proximal step onto the active face (the steepest descent\ndirection on the face, in the metric of H+E ), stored as x-xold .\nReturns false if no projection was done. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes