 implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine daqp_ldp2qp_solution ( work ) type ( daqp_workspace ), intent ( inout ) :: work !! workspace integer ( ip ) :: i if ( work % has_v ) then do i = 1 , work % n work % x ( i ) = work % x ( i ) - work % v ( i ) end do end if if ( work % rmode /= rinv_none ) call apply_Rinv ( work , work % x ) do i = 1 , work % n_active work % lam_star ( i ) = work % lam_star ( i ) * work % scaling ( work % WS ( i )) end do end subroutine daqp_ldp2qp_solution","tags":"","url":"proc/daqp_ldp2qp_solution.html"},{"title":"invert_R – daqp-fortran","text":"private  subroutine invert_R(work) Invert the packed factor R in place. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace Calls proc~~invert_r~~CallsGraph proc~invert_r invert_R proc~ridx~2 ridx proc~invert_r->proc~ridx~2 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~invert_r~~CalledByGraph proc~invert_r invert_R proc~finish_rinv finish_Rinv proc~finish_rinv->proc~invert_r proc~finish_rinv_qp finish_Rinv_qp proc~finish_rinv_qp->proc~finish_rinv proc~update_r update_R proc~update_r->proc~finish_rinv proc~retry_avi_with_reduced_rho retry_avi_with_reduced_rho proc~retry_avi_with_reduced_rho->proc~update_r proc~update_ldp_core update_ldp_core proc~update_ldp_core->proc~finish_rinv_qp 