stall proc~daqp_refresh_soft_weights->proc~daqp_eq_restore proc~daqp_set_primal_start daqp_set_primal_start proc~daqp_set_primal_start->proc~daqp_eq_install proc~daqp_set_primal_start->proc~daqp_eq_restore proc~daqp_set_working_set daqp_set_working_set proc~daqp_set_working_set->proc~daqp_eq_install proc~daqp_set_working_set->proc~daqp_eq_restore proc~daqp_solve daqp_solve proc~daqp_solve->proc~daqp_eq_install proc~daqp_solve->proc~daqp_eq_restore proc~daqp_update_ldp daqp_update_ldp proc~daqp_solve->proc~daqp_update_ldp proc~daqp_update_ldp->proc~daqp_eq_restore proc~daqp_update_ldp->proc~daqp_eq_update proc~daqp_update_ldp->proc~daqp_eq_deactivate proc~free_daqp_eq free_daqp_eq proc~free_daqp_eq->proc~daqp_eq_restore proc~daqp_eq_deactivate->proc~free_daqp_eq proc~daqp_quadprog daqp_quadprog proc~daqp_quadprog->proc~daqp_solve proc~daqp_setup daqp_setup proc~daqp_quadprog->proc~daqp_setup proc~daqp_set_soft_weights daqp_set_soft_weights proc~daqp_set_soft_weights->proc~daqp_refresh_soft_weights proc~daqp_setup->proc~daqp_set_primal_start proc~daqp_setup->proc~daqp_update_ldp proc~set_primal_start daqp_type%set_primal_start proc~set_primal_start->proc~daqp_set_primal_start proc~set_working_set daqp_type%set_working_set proc~set_working_set->proc~daqp_set_working_set proc~solve daqp_type%solve proc~solve->proc~daqp_refresh_soft_weights proc~solve->proc~daqp_solve proc~solve->proc~set_working_set proc~update daqp_type%update proc~update->proc~daqp_update_ldp proc~daqp_avi daqp_avi proc~daqp_avi->proc~daqp_quadprog proc~set_soft_weights daqp_type%set_soft_weights proc~set_soft_weights->proc~daqp_set_soft_weights proc~setup daqp_type%setup proc~setup->proc~daqp_setup Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine swap_problem ( a , b ) type ( daqp_problem ), intent ( inout ) :: a !! first type ( daqp_problem ), intent ( inout ) :: b !! second call swap_int ( a % n , b % n ) call swap_int ( a % m , b % m ) call swap_int ( a % ms , b % ms ) call swap_log ( a % has_H , b % has_H ) call swap_log ( a % has_f , b % has_f ) call swap_log ( a % has_sense , b % has_sense ) call swap_int ( a % problem_type , b % problem_type ) call swap_r2 ( a % Hc , b % Hc ) call swap_r1 ( a % Rf , b % Rf ) call swap_r1 ( a % f , b % f ) call swap_r2 ( a % At , b % At ) call swap_r1 ( a % bupper , b % bupper ) call swap_r1 ( a % blower , b % blower ) call swap_i1 ( a % sense , b % sense ) call swap_int ( a % nh , b % nh ) call swap_i1 ( a % break_points , b % break_points ) end subroutine swap_problem","tags":"","url":"proc/swap_problem.html"},{"title":"daqp_eq_elim – daqp-fortran","text":"Elimination of equality constraints, before the QP is turned into an LDP:\na translation of eq_elim.c of DAQP v0.10.3 (Copyright (c) 2022 Daniel Arnström, MIT licence). Changed from the\noriginal: translated to Fortran, 1-based indexing. The equality constraints A_E x = b_E are eliminated through x = xp + W w , where the columns of W span the null space of A_E (from the QR factorization A_E' = Q [R; 0] of the normalized rows) and xp is a particular solution. With x = xp + W w the remaining constraints\nbecome constraints on w (the simple bounds turning into general\nconstraints), and the reduced problem is posed in one of three ways\n( eq%path ): eq_path_ldp : if Z'HZ = L L' is positive definite, W = Z L&#94;{-T} gives W'HW = I , and xp is the minimizer over the equality constraints, so\n  that the reduced problem is min 0.5||w||&#94;2 . For a diagonal (positive)\n  Hessian, the QR is formed in the metric of H instead. eq_path_qp : otherwise, W = Z and the reduced problem keeps the\n  Hessian Z'HZ and the linear term Z'(H xp + f) . eq_path_lp : for an LP, W = Z and the linear term is Z'f . The reduced problem is an ordinary problem, whose LDP is formed and solved\nby the usual routines: it is swapped into the workspace (installed) while\nit is formed or solved, and the workspace describes the original problem\notherwise. Matrices are in upstream's (row-major) memory order: V(:,k) is\nthe k-th Householder vector (then Z ), W(:,i) is the i-th row of W . Uses daqp_types daqp_kinds module~~daqp_eq_elim~~UsesGraph module~daqp_eq_elim daqp_eq_elim module~daqp_kinds daqp_kinds module~daqp_eq_elim->module~daqp_kinds module~daqp_types daqp_types module~daqp_eq_elim->module~daqp_types iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~daqp_kinds->iso_fortran_env module~daqp_types->module~daqp_kinds module~daqp_types->iso_fortran_env Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~daqp_eq_elim~~UsedByGraph module~daqp_eq_elim daqp_eq_elim module~daqp_core daqp_core module~daqp_core->module~daqp_eq_elim module~daqp_module daqp_module module~daqp_module->module~daqp_core Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Abstract Interfaces abstract interface public  function update_ldp_proc(mask, work) Forms the LDP of the problem in the workspace. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: mask type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work Return Value integer(kind=ip) Functions private  function eq_chol (A, n, zero_tol) Cholesky factorization A = L L' (lower, row major: A(j,i) , j <= i , in\nplace), with the rows in blocks of four. Returns false if A is not\npositive definite (a pivot below zero_tol , or relative to the largest pivot). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: A (:,:) matrix; factor on output integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: n dimension real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: zero_tol tolerance Return Value logical private pure function eq_dot (a, b, n) Dot product, summed in order. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: a (:) first vector real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: b (:) second vector integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: n length Return Value real(kind=wp) private pure function eq_is_candidate (work, i) Whether the general constraint i is an equality that can be eliminated\n(the same criteria as the detection of equal bounds). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(in) :: work workspace integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: i constraint Return Value logical private pure function eq_count_candidates (work) Number of equality candidates. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(in) :: work workspace Return Value integer(kind=ip) private pure function eq_is_diagonal (qp, zero_tol) Whether H is diagonal. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_problem ), intent(in) :: qp the problem real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: zero_tol tolerance Return Value logical private pure function eq_is_worthwhile (work, n_eq) Whether eliminating n_eq equalities is expected to pay off. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(in) :: work workspace integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: n_eq number of equality candidates Return Value logical public  function daqp_eq_wanted (work, mask) Whether the problem in the workspace is to be reduced for an update with mask ( settings%eq_reduction ; auto only with daqp_update_eliminate ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(in) :: work workspace integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: mask update mask Return Value logical private  function eq_same_candidates (work) Whether the equality candidates are the ones that the reduction was formed for. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(in) :: work workspace Return Value logical private pure function eq_is_symmetric (qp, zero_tol) Whether H is symmetric (for an AVI). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_problem ), intent(in) :: qp the problem real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: zero_tol tolerance Return Value logical private  function eq_split_flat (qp, Z, n, nz, cid, nc, zero_tol, Hr) result(r) Split Z ( n x nz ) into [Z1 Z2] , with Z2 zero in the rows cid (the\nvariables with curvature), so that H*Z2 = 0 exactly. Forms Hr = blockdiag(Z1'HZ1, 0) and returns the dimension of Z1 . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_problem ), intent(in) :: qp the problem real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: Z (:,:) null-space basis (columns) integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: n number of variables integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: nz dimension of the null space integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: cid (:) variables with curvature integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: nc number of them real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: zero_tol tolerance real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: Hr (:,:) reduced Hessian Return Value integer(kind=ip) private  function eq_build_reduction (work) result(flag) Form the reduction of the problem in the workspace: the factorizations, the\nreduced constraints and the storage of the reduced problem. Returns 0 if\nnothing can be eliminated, or if a soft constraint would be left out. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace Return Value integer(kind=ip) private pure function eq_value (work, id) Value of equality id (the upper bound, unless it is active at its lower one). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(in) :: work workspace integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: id constraint Return Value real(kind=wp) private  function eq_reduce_rhs (work, warm) result(flag) The part that depends on b and f : the particular solution xp , the\nlinear term of the reduced problem ( eq_path_qp , eq_path_lp ), and the\nshifted bounds. With warm , the responses to b_E and f are used if\nfew equalities have a nonzero right-hand side.\nReturns 1, or a negative exit flag if the implied constraints are violated. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace logical, intent(in) :: warm the reduction was not formed anew Return Value integer(kind=ip) public  function daqp_eq_install (work) Swap the reduced problem into the workspace. Returns whether it is installed\n(by this call). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace Return Value logical public  function daqp_eq_update (work, mask, update_ldp) result(flag) Form or update the reduction of the problem in the workspace, and the LDP\nof the reduced problem (with update_ldp ). Returns eq_not_reduced if\nnothing can be eliminated, a negative exit flag if the equality constraints\ncannot be satisfied, and the return value of update_ldp otherwise. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: mask update mask procedure( update_ldp_proc ) :: update_ldp forms the LDP of the installed problem Return Value integer(kind=ip) Subroutines private pure subroutine eq_reflect (v, tau, k, n, y) y <-- (I - tau v v') y on the indices >= k ( v(k) = 1 implicitly). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: v (:) Householder vector real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tau Householder scalar integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: k first index integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: n length real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: y (:) vector private  subroutine eq_apply_QT_many (V, tau, nr, n, Y, cnt) Y <-- Q'Y for the cnt columns of Y (length n ), with the reflectors 1..nr (four vectors per pass over a reflector). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: V (:,:) Householder vectors (columns) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tau (:) Householder scalars integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: nr number of reflectors integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: n length of the vectors real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: Y (:,:) vectors (columns) integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: cnt number of vectors private  subroutine eq_accumulate_Z (V, tau, nr, n) Z = Q(:,nr+1:n) , accumulated in the columns nr+1..n of V (four at a time). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: V (:,:) Householder vectors; Z on output real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tau (:) Householder scalars integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: nr number of reflectors integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: n dimension private  subroutine eq_gemm_tn (n, p, q, X, Y, C, upper) C(j,i) = X(:,i).Y(:,j) for vectors of length n . With upper , only j >= i is computed, and then mirrored. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: n length of the vectors integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: p number of vectors in X integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: q number of vectors in Y real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: X (:,:) vectors (columns) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: Y (:,:) vectors (columns) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: C (:,:) products logical, intent(in) :: upper only the upper triangle (mirrored) private  subroutine eq_twoside (B, n, V, tau, nr, p) B <-- P_k B P_k for k = 1..nr , for a symmetric B (lower triangle,\nrow major: B(j,i) , j <= i ). Only the trailing blocks are updated. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: B (:,:) symmetric matrix (lower triangle) integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: n dimension real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: V (:,:) Householder vectors real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: tau (:) Householder scalars integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: nr number of reflectors real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: p (:) scratch (n) private  subroutine eq_trsm_rows (L, nz, X, cnt) Rows X(:,r) <-- X(:,r) L&#94;{-T} (solves L x' = x' ), for cnt rows\n( L lower, row major: L(k,j) , k <= j ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: L (:,:) Cholesky factor integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: nz dimension real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: X (:,:) rows (columns of X) integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: cnt number of rows private  subroutine eq_rows_times_W (At, ids, ms, cnt, n, W, nz, C) C(:,i) = W' a_{ids(i)} for the general constraints ids (the rows of A times W , with W(:,k) the k-th row of W ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: At (:,:) rows of A (columns) integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: ids (:) constraints integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: ms number of simple bounds integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: cnt number of constraints integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: n number of variables real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: W (:,:) null-space basis (rows as columns) integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: nz number of reduced variables real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: C (:,:) products (columns) private  subroutine eq_hess_times (qp, metric, x, y) y <-- H x (dense, or diagonal if metric ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_problem ), intent(in) :: qp the problem logical, intent(in) :: metric H is diagonal real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x (:) vector real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: y (:) H x private  subroutine eq_free_reduced_ldp (eq) Free the LDP of the reduced problem (not the reduced problem itself). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_eq_data ), intent(inout) :: eq elimination private  subroutine eq_allocate_reduced_ldp (eq, nb) Storage of the LDP of the reduced problem (which has no simple bounds). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_eq_data ), intent(inout) :: eq elimination integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: nb number of binary constraints private  subroutine eq_free_rhs_cache (eq) Free the cached responses to the right-hand side. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_eq_data ), intent(inout) :: eq elimination private  subroutine eq_free_reduction (eq) Free the reduction (and the reduced problem). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_eq_data ), intent(inout) :: eq elimination private  subroutine eq_allocate_reduction (eq, n, m, ms) Storage that only depends on the dimensions of the original problem. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_eq_data ), intent(inout) :: eq elimination integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: n dimensions of the original problem integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: m dimensions of the original problem integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: ms dimensions of the original problem private  subroutine eq_build_qr (work, zero_tol) Householder QR of A_E' ( A_E H&#94;{-1/2} if metric ), left-looking in\npanels of four candidates. Candidates that are (numerically) linearly\ndependent on the ones before are not eliminated. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: zero_tol tolerance private  subroutine eq_rhs_column (work, k) Response of xp to a unit right-hand side of eliminated equality k (in eq_path_ldp ), stored in eq%cols(k)%v = [xp_k, H xp_k, shifts] . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace integer(kind=ip), intent(in) :: k eliminated equality private  subroutine eq_rhs_f (work) Response of xp to f ( eq_path_ldp ): xf = -W W'f , gf = H xf + f , df = -A xf . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace private  subroutine eq_swap_ldp (work) Exchange the LDP of the workspace with work%eq%other (no copy). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace public  subroutine daqp_eq_restore (work) Swap the original problem back into the workspace. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace public  subroutine daqp_eq_deactivate (work) Give up the reduction (the LDP of the original problem then has to be formed). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace private  subroutine eq_compute_lam_eq (work, x, lam) Multipliers of the eliminated equalities, from the stationarity condition A_E' lam_E = -(H x + f + A_K' lam_K) . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace (with the reduced problem installed) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x (:) solution of the original problem real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: lam (:) multipliers public  subroutine daqp_eq_expand (work, x, fval, lam) Turn the result of the installed reduced problem into the result of the\noriginal problem, and carry its working set over to the original constraints. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace (with the reduced problem installed) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: x (:) solution (of size n of the original problem) real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: fval objective (of the reduced problem on input) real(kind=wp), intent(inout), optional :: lam (:) multipliers (of the reduced problem on input) public  subroutine daqp_eq_set_primal_start (work, x) Set the starting iterate of the reduced problem from x of the original one. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x (:) iterate of the original problem public  subroutine free_daqp_eq (work) Free the elimination (restoring the original problem first). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( daqp_workspace ), intent(inout) :: work workspace","tags":"","url":"module/daqp_eq_elim.html"},{"title":"daqp_core – daqp-fortran","text":"The Fortran port of the DAQP solver (dual active-set method for dense\nconvex quadratic programs, with branch and bound for binary constraints,\nhierarchical QPs, affine variational inequalities, and a proximal-point\nouter loop for semidefinite problems and LPs). This module is a modern Fortran translation of the C code of DAQP v0.10.3\n(Copyright (c) 2022 Daniel Arnström, MIT licence): daqp.c , auxiliary.c , factorization.c , utils.c , api.c , daqp_prox.c , bnb.c , hierarchical.c , and avi.c (the elimination of equalities, eq_elim.c , is in daqp_eq_elim ). Changed from the original: translated\nto Fortran, 1-based indexing, allocatable components instead of pointers\n(see daqp_types for the storage). The QP is min  0.5 x'Hx + f'x\ns.t. blower(1:ms) <= x(1:ms)  <= bupper(1:ms)\n     blower(ms+1:) <= A x     <= bupper(ms+1:) It is turned into the least-distance problem (LDP) min 0.5 ||u||&#94;2 s.t. dlower <= M u <= dupper , with H = R'R , u = R x + R'\\f and M = A R&#94;{-1} , which is solved by a dual active-set\nmethod that updates the LDL' factors of the working set's Gram matrix. Uses ieee_arithmetic iso_fortran_env daqp_types daqp_eq_elim daqp_kinds module~~daqp_core~~UsesGraph module~daqp_core daqp_core ieee_arithmetic ieee_arithmetic module~daqp_core->ieee_arithmetic iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~daqp_core->iso_fortran_env module~daqp_eq_elim daqp_eq_elim module~daqp_core->module~daqp_eq_elim module~daqp_kinds daqp_kinds module~daqp_core->module~daqp_kinds module~daqp_types daqp_types module~daq